  "scope": "The fixed 32-instruction physical machine scans every original stored numerator with the actual padded binary-zero submachine, preserves each original row/address, and allocates the ordered Boolean mask through real recursive calls. The exact old BinaryFractionalDispatch.zeroMask fields are returned on the same paid physical run. Bounds use only original row count and stored field-bit lengths, including the final halt attempt. Eight physical cases include empty and padded zero, nonzero, mixed order, duplicate records and raw zero denominators. Initial heap representations and address widths remain explicit. This is the zero-mask stage of outer dispatch; kept-adjacency construction, demand branch selection and whole dispatch remain separate. The original dispatch definition is imported unchanged, bringing seven old mathematical modules into the selected reference closure at integration."
